<task id="011" project="spaarkeai-compose-r3">
  <metadata>
    <title>FR-09/FR-10 explicit load-time paraId carry (hidden node attr) + split-minting via `@tiptap/extension-unique-id`</title>
    <phase>1 E2</phase>
    <gate>blocked</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>W1-E2</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>010</deps>
    <tags>frontend,tiptap,pcf</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2-3 days</estimated-effort>
    <assigned>unassigned</assigned>
    <started></started>
    <completed></completed>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Implement FR-09 + FR-10 on the client: carry the server-minted `w14:paraId`s (from task 010's
    Load response) into the editor and keep them stable across edits. Two halves.
    (1) FR-09 — on Load, set each paragraph's paraId as a **hidden ProseMirror node attribute** via
    an **explicit transaction** immediately after `setContent`. S2 proved `@tiptap/extension-unique-id`
    does NOT auto-assign ids to `setContent`-loaded nodes, so the server pre-parse owns load-time ids
    and the client must stamp them explicitly. The ids are node attributes only — NOT rendered to the
    DOM (no `data-*` attribute, no visual output).
    (2) FR-10 — configure `@tiptap/extension-unique-id` (3.28.0, MIT) for the `paragraph` type with
    `attributeName: 'paraId'` and an OOXML-shaped `generateID` (an 8-hex `ST_LongHexNumber` `&lt;
    0x80000000` generator). On a paragraph split, UniqueID's built-in dedup keeps the original id on
    one half and re-mints a fresh id on the other; untouched paragraphs keep their ids. **NO custom
    minting plugin** — the extension's built-in dedup is the mechanism (S2 simplification). The paraId
    carry lives in `docxBridge.ts`; the editor/extension config lives in `ComposeEditor.tsx`.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Senior front-end engineer fluent in TipTap v3 / ProseMirror (nodes, attributes, explicit
    transactions, `setContent` semantics) and the MIT TipTap extension ecosystem, working in the
    `Spaarke.Compose.Components` shared library. Careful about license provenance
    (`@tiptap/extension-*` MIT vs `@tiptap-pro/*` forbidden) and about keeping node identity off the
    rendered DOM.
  </role>

  <goal>
    The editor carries the server-minted paraIds as hidden `paragraph` node attributes immediately
    after mount (set by an explicit transaction, not left to auto-assign), and keeps them stable
    across editing: untouched paragraphs retain their ids; a split yields two distinct paraIds, one
    equal to the original, the other freshly minted OOXML-shaped — all via `@tiptap/extension-unique-id`
    3.28.0 (MIT) with `attributeName: 'paraId'` + an 8-hex `&lt; 0x80000000` `generateID`, and NO
    custom plugin. Client tests assert: ids present on nodes after mount, ids absent from the rendered
    DOM, split-minting behaviour (one kept + one re-minted), and that the resolved package is
    `@tiptap/extension-unique-id` (MIT), never `@tiptap-pro/*`.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      E2 client half of the paraId identity substrate (design §5, §8 LOAD/EDIT pipeline). Task 010
      (server pre-parse) mints/collects the ids and projects a `paraId → paragraph` map onto the
      Load response; this task carries those ids into ProseMirror node attributes and configures the
      minting extension for in-editor split/merge. S2 (spike) is the validated recipe: headless
      TipTap v3 + `@tiptap/extension-unique-id` 3.28.0, untouched paraIds preserved, split keeps one
      id + re-mints the other via the extension's built-in dedup — **no custom plugin**, and load-time
      ids set explicitly because UniqueID does not auto-assign to `setContent`-loaded nodes. mammoth
      flattens `.docx` to HTML and discards paraId (`docxBridge.ts`), so the ids arrive from the server
      map, not from the imported HTML. TipTap open-sourced `UniqueID` (formerly Pro) under MIT in
      June 2025 — allowed, but the resolved dependency MUST be `@tiptap/extension-unique-id`, NEVER
      `@tiptap-pro/*` (owner rule 2026-07-14; NFR-03). ids are node attributes only and MUST NOT
      render to the DOM (FR-09). This task is client-only (no BFF/publish-size surface) and
      parallel-safe.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/utils/docxBridge.ts — carry the server paraId map into the editor: after setContent, run an explicit transaction stamping each paragraph node's `paraId` attribute (FR-09); do NOT rely on auto-assign</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeEditor.tsx — configure `@tiptap/extension-unique-id` for `paragraph` with `attributeName: 'paraId'` + OOXML-shaped `generateID` (FR-10); ensure the paraId attribute is NOT rendered to the DOM</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/package.json — add `@tiptap/extension-unique-id` 3.28.0 (MIT); verify it resolves to `@tiptap/extension-*`, never `@tiptap-pro/*`</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/types/compose-contracts.ts — the Load-response contract shape; consume task 010's additive paraId-map field (mirror-first, do not fork the schema)</file>
      <file role="reference">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r3/notes/spikes/ — S2 (paraId carry-through in TipTap; split re-mints one half; server owns load-time ids; generateID OOXML-shaped); the validated recipe this task productionizes</file>
      <file role="design">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r3/design.md §5 (E2 paraId identity — hidden node attr, UniqueID config, Word-regeneration caveat), §2 (Current State — mammoth discards paraId; anchoring model compose-contracts.ts:108-115), §8 (LOAD/EDIT pipeline), §10 (reuse map — MIT `@tiptap/extension-unique-id`, NO TipTap Pro)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="010" status="pending">Server pre-parse mints/collects the `w14:paraId`s and projects the ordered `paraId → paragraph` map onto the Load response. This task consumes that map to stamp node attributes; the map's contract shape is the input.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="FR-09">paraIds are set as hidden `paragraph` node attributes via an EXPLICIT transaction immediately after `setContent` (not left to UniqueID auto-assign — S2). The ids MUST NOT be rendered to the DOM (no `data-*`/visible output).</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-10">Split/merge minting is handled by `@tiptap/extension-unique-id` (3.28.0, MIT) configured for `paragraph` with `attributeName: 'paraId'` and an OOXML-shaped `generateID` (8-hex `&lt; 0x80000000`). On split, one half keeps the id, the other is re-minted. NO custom minting plugin.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-03 / owner rule 2026-07-14 / project MUST-NOT">The extension MUST resolve to `@tiptap/extension-unique-id` (MIT), NEVER `@tiptap-pro/*`. No TipTap product feature (paid or unpaid) and no AGPL code. Verify the resolved package + license before/after install.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-10 / ADR-021 / ADR-028">Any new/changed UI uses Fluent v9 + dark mode; client fetches use `@spaarke/auth`. (This task is mostly editor-config; applies to any surfaced affordance.)</constraint>
    <constraint source="mirror-first / project">Consume task 010's additive paraId-map field from the mirrored Load-response contract in `compose-contracts.ts`; do NOT invent a parallel client schema.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-06 / ADR-038">Client behaviour (ids on nodes after mount, ids absent from DOM, split-minting, license resolution) is covered by client tests; the full through-the-wire proof rides with tasks 010/012's seam slices. No `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`-style false-greens.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>TipTap v3 / ProseMirror node attributes + explicit transactions; `@tiptap/extension-unique-id` (MIT) config + built-in split dedup; `w14:paraId` OOXML-shaped id generation; license provenance</topic>
