  </outputs>

  <justification>
    <existing>The editor already configures TipTap MIT-base extensions in `ComposeEditor.tsx` and converts mammoth HTML in `docxBridge.ts`, but neither carries a stable paragraph identity — anchors are fuzzy `textPattern`/`paragraphHint`/session-`spanId` (`compose-contracts.ts:108-115`). No existing paraId carry or minting on the client. Verified by grep across `Spaarke.Compose.Components/src`.</existing>
    <extension>This EXTENDS existing files (`docxBridge.ts`, `ComposeEditor.tsx`, `package.json`) rather than adding a component; the only new dependency is the MIT `@tiptap/extension-unique-id`, whose split/merge dedup is exactly the minting mechanism we need (S2) — building a custom plugin instead would be reinventing a maintained MIT extension (rejected per S2 simplification).</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without the client carry, the server-minted ids (task 010) never reach the editor, so edited editor paragraphs cannot be mapped back to original OOXML paragraphs on save (FR-12) and E2/E3 anchors stay fuzzy. Concrete failing contract: FR-09 acceptance "editor doc nodes carry `paraId` immediately after mount" and FR-10 "splitting a paragraph yields two distinct paraIds, one equal to the original" are unmet, blocking the E1 splice (task 020) and paraId anchoring (task 012).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <acceptance-criteria testable="true">
    <criterion testable="true">Editor `paragraph` nodes carry a `paraId` attribute immediately after mount, matching the server pre-parse map in document order (FR-09 acceptance).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The paraId is a hidden node attribute — it is NOT rendered to the DOM (no `data-*`/visible attribute); a test inspects the rendered HTML and finds no paraId (FR-09 acceptance).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`@tiptap/extension-unique-id` 3.28.0 is configured for `paragraph` with `attributeName: 'paraId'` and an OOXML-shaped `generateID` (8-hex `&lt; 0x80000000`).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Splitting a paragraph yields two distinct paraIds, one equal to the original id and the other freshly minted and OOXML-valid — via the extension's built-in dedup, with NO custom minting plugin (FR-10 acceptance, per S2).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Untouched paragraphs keep their paraIds across unrelated edits.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The resolved dependency is `@tiptap/extension-unique-id` (MIT); a check confirms it is NOT `@tiptap-pro/*` and no AGPL code is added (NFR-03 / owner rule).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Client tests exist and pass; the shared-lib build is green.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

